# Postgres. Dev container suggested in README (port 5434 to avoid clashing with
# longhaul's 5433).
DATABASE_URL=postgres://recipus:recipus@localhost:5434/recipus

# --- Auth -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Recipus authenticates every request itself and never trusts the network.
# In production Nginx Proxy Manager sits in front, Authelia does the 2FA, and
# NPM injects both the proxy secret and the authenticated username.
#
# PROXY_AUTH_SECRET must be set before deploy or every request is rejected and
# the app looks dead. There is deliberately no default.
PROXY_AUTH_SECRET=

# Header NPM uses to pass the Authelia-authenticated username through.
PROXY_USER_HEADER=Remote-User

# Dev only: when set, requests with no proxy headers are treated as this user
# so you can run the app locally without Authelia in front. Ignored entirely
# when NODE_ENV=production, so leaving it in a production .env is harmless —
# but leave it out anyway, so nobody has to check that claim under pressure.
DEV_AUTH_USER=anders

# --- Reading with Claude: the shim ------------------------------------------
# Everything in this app that asks a model something — the LLM fallback for
# recipe pages with no JSON-LD, and reading a photo/clump of text into list
# rows — goes through one small service on the beelink. It holds the Claude
# Code credential, so the household's subscription pays rather than a metered
# API key, and no credential of Claude's own ever lives in this repo. The
# service lives in agentic-os (`shim/`), not here; see docs/deploy.md.
#
# BOTH must be set or nothing is asked. Unset is a supported state, not a
# broken one: URL import still works for every site publishing
# schema.org/Recipe JSON-LD, text and speech fall back to the deterministic
# parser, and only reading an image has no fallback and answers 503.
#
# The shim binds 0.0.0.0 on 8301, because this container lives in a bridge
# network and cannot reach the host's loopback. The host half is `beelink.host`
# where that name resolves, and 192.168.50.197 where it does not.
# AI_SHIM_URL=http://beelink.host:8301
#
# The same value as SHIM_INGEST_SECRET in agentic-os's .env (the repo root, not
# shim/) — a mismatch is a 401 there and a silent degradation here.
# `openssl rand -hex 32`.
# AI_SHIM_SECRET=

# --- Catalog seeding --------------------------------------------------------
# The server re-seeds categories, the Swedish catalog and the starter list on
# every boot (src/instrumentation.ts). The seed is idempotent and never
# overwrites what the household owns — has_at_home, use_count, last_used_at —
# so this is how a deploy that adds catalog items ships them.
#
# Unset means: on in production, off in dev (use `pnpm db:seed` locally).
# Set to 1 or 0 to force it either way.
# SEED_ON_BOOT=

# --- Retention -------------------------------------------------------------
# The one thing in this app that DELETES. Runs on boot and then daily, and takes
# everything past 30 days: the op log, tombstoned entries, removed recipe
# additions, deleted lists and recipes, spent suggestion dismissals.
#
# Purchases are never pruned — they are the only record that the household
# bought something, and the sole input to the cadence engine and the statistics
# screen.
#
# Same default shape as SEED_ON_BOOT (on in production, off in dev) but for a
# sharper reason: a dev database left on a laptop for two months would lose its
# old tombstones on the next `pnpm dev`, which is correct behaviour arriving at a
# startling moment. Set to 1 to exercise it locally, 0 to hold it off in
# production.
# PRUNE_ON_BOOT=

# --- Who the household is ---------------------------------------------------
#
# Comma-separated Authelia usernames. Authelia fronts every service on the
# beelink, so without this ANY account it authenticates — including one created
# for an unrelated app — is a full member here: it can read the list, and it can
# call merge_catalog_items, which tombstones a vara and permanently re-points
# future recipe matching.
#
# Unset means "anyone Authelia lets through", which is the behaviour this app
# already shipped with. That default is kept on purpose: failing closed would
# lock the household out of its own shopping list on the next Watchtower pull,
# remotely, with an SSH session as the only fix. Production logs a warning until
# this is set. Set it.
# HOUSEHOLD_USERS=anders,jannica

# --- Voice: adding to the list by saying it ---------------------------------
#
# Two doors, both mounted OUTSIDE Authelia because their callers are machines
# with no browser session — and therefore both carrying their own lock. Neither
# falls back to "unguarded" when unconfigured: an unset secret makes the
# endpoint answer 503, never 200.
#
# Home Assistant (/api/voice/utterance). The Swedish half, and the only one that
# CAN be Swedish: Alexa supports 17 custom-skill locales and sv-SE is not among
# them, so a self-hosted Whisper pipeline is the sole route by which "lägg till
# mjölk" arrives as those words. Generate with `openssl rand -hex 32` and put
# the same value in the HA rest_command's Authorization header.
# VOICE_INGEST_SECRET=
#
# Who a spoken add is attributed to. Ops carry an actor and the entry sheet says
# it out loud, so this must name a real household member — the same string
# Authelia authenticates that person as.
# VOICE_ACTOR=anders
#
# Alexa (/api/alexa). English only, for the reason above; English words reach
# the Swedish catalog through the seeded aliases in catalog_item_aliases.
# ALEXA_SKILL_ID is checked against every request: the signature verifier proves
# a request came from Amazon, but NOT that it came from YOUR skill, so without
# this any skill in the world could write to the household's list.
# ALEXA_SKILL_ID=amzn1.ask.skill.<uuid>
# ALEXA_ACTOR=anders
# Which list a spoken add lands on. Unset means the household's first list, in
# the same order the switcher draws.
# ALEXA_LIST_ID=

# --- Production only --------------------------------------------------------
# On the beelink these are set in ~/services/recipus/.env, not here:
#   DATABASE_URL=postgres://recipus:<password>@postgres:5432/recipus
#   PROXY_AUTH_SECRET=<openssl rand -hex 32, matching the NPM injected header>
#   AI_SHIM_URL=http://beelink.host:8301
#   AI_SHIM_SECRET=<the shim's SHIM_INGEST_SECRET, verbatim>
# and DEV_AUTH_USER is omitted. See docs/deploy.md.
